        <span itemprop="subject">Table 1</span>
        <span itemprop="definition">shows that the microporous polyethylene membrane of Examples 1 to 4 had shutdown temperatures of 135° C. or lower, air permeability change ratios of 10,000 sec/100 cm 3 /° C. or more, and meltdown temperatures of 150° C. or higher, exhibiting low shutdown temperatures, high shutdown speeds and high meltdown temperatures. They further had excellent permeability, mechanical strength and heat shrinkage resistance.</span>
        <meta itemprop="num_attr" content="0197">
